w(Bg,"Gear List","Budget/Gear List",gs('1_4TK1viaU-q1dS8aaruxTwfIRtnY37vshthcPHtHuew'),'sheet','2018-05-25','high',['gear','packing-list','budget-finance','bike-maintenance'],"Four-tab gear workbook: one rider's packing list, a who-owns-what matrix, an inventory of inherited boxes, and a per-rider to-buy list with costs. Practical template for 2027 gear planning.","""
## Sample personal packing list (Bethany)
Clothes: 2 jerseys, 2 bike shorts, 2 normal shorts (one nice pair for teaching), casual shirt, nice shirt, leggings, 2 sports bras, underwear, ankle socks, 1 light hiking socks, swimsuit, fleece, rain jacket. Shoes: Tevas, trail sneakers, bike shoes (maybe real shoes for teaching: probably not). Camping: sleeping bag, sleeping pad, Swiss army knife. Toiletries: shampoo, conditioner, body wash.

## Stuff we have (x = owns)
Team asked to mark what they own. Sleeping pad and bag owned by nearly everyone (Annie, Bethany, Delia, Kate, Lisa, Matthew); tents: Annie and Bethany each a 2-person; Matthew owns helmet, bike shorts, socks, pillow; Bethany owns pump, helmet, bottle cages; Delia pump and seat/handlebar bag; An bike shorts and socks.

## Inventory of inherited boxes (from prior teams)
- Box 1: general medical supplies, pepper spray, lots of road maps, 2 very big sleeping bags, sleeping pad, hydration vitamins/electrolytes, frame pump, thank-you cards, 2 lanterns, towel, one walkie talkie, bicycle maintenance and repair book, 2 laptops, floor pump, one tent with no poles.
- Box 2 (teaching/tools): 2 Rubik's cubes, wire stripper, scissors, 2 bags hot glue guns, sterile scalpels, matches, cow eye dissection guide, magnets, batteries (some dead), resistors, 18 goggles, 5 unused 9V batteries, double-sided tape, gates and switches, iron filings, electrical tape, pliers, compass, small stove, X-Acto knives, playing cards, super glue.
- Box 3 (kitchen): plastic spoons, paper towels, bike seat bag, lots of sunscreen, bug spray, soap, chip clips, spatula, ladle, bowls, can opener, pot, big bowl, pan, knife, 2 fuel canisters.
- Box 4 (bike/camp): pot lid, bike rack part, walkie talkies, CO2 cylinder, tent stakes (no poles), small pots, 5 rearview mirrors, bungees, bike locks without keys, 3 spare tubes, bottle cage, electrolytes, reflective tape, emergency blanket, rope, sporks.

## Stuff we need (per rider, with prices)
Saddle bag $17.99 each (An, Annie, Bethany, Kate, Lisa, Matt); biking tights $33; phone mount $15.98; UV jersey $25; bike pants $33.99; sleeping bag $69.51; Therm-a-Rest pad $44.95; cycling socks $13.99; rain pants $37; sleeping bag liner $15.95; sweatbands $9.99; tent ground tarps $14.99 (x2-3); day pack $20.99; quick-dry towel $32; 100 thank-you cards with envelopes $17.99; bike multitool $9; stamps; bike strips (mrtuffy.com). Totals per rider: An $321.94, Kate $109.56, Lisa $36.97, Delia $30.56, others about $17.99. Note: team agreed to mass-buy insect repellent and split the cost.
""")
